        "After years of conflict over the authority of Scripture and sexuality in the Episcopal Church and the Anglican Church of Canada, conservative dioceses and congregations meet in Bedford, Texas, in June 2009 to constitute the Anglican Church in North America, with Robert Duncan as its first archbishop. Recognized by many Anglican provinces of the Global South, though not a member of the Anglican Communion, it gathered evangelical, charismatic and Anglo-Catholic Anglicans and includes congregations in Mexico, Guatemala and Cuba.",
