        "Jim and Tammy Faye Bakker's PTL ('Praise the Lord') Club, a Pentecostal talk show, had built a satellite network and Heritage USA, a Christian theme park near Fort Mill, South Carolina, visited by millions. In March 1987 Jim Bakker resigns after a sexual and financial scandal; investigators found that he had sold far more 'lifetime partnerships' than could be honoured, and in 1989 he was convicted of fraud. Together with the 1988 scandal of Jimmy Swaggart, it shook public trust in televangelists in the United States and in Latin America, where both had large audiences.",
